From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: babarot <b4b4r07@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:51:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Stack in-app toasts instead of queueing them

Only one in-app toast is shown at a time. A notification that arrives
while a toast is up waits in a queue until that toast closes, so when
agents in several panes or machines finish at about the same time, the
later ones show up only after the earlier ones are gone.

Show each toast at once instead, stacked on the ones already up: the
newest sits at the edge ui.toast.herdr.position names and older ones
move away from it. Each toast counts its own duration from when it
appears and closes alone, and the rest close the gap. Up to 5 are shown;
a sixth closes the oldest, and one that no longer fits on the screen is
left out along with the older ones. A new notification from a pane
still replaces that pane's toast, and retiring an endpoint closes all of
its toasts.

Clicking a toast closes only that one (focusing its pane, if it has
one); the open-notification key opens the newest. The mobile banner has
room for one row, so it shows the newest only.
